    "https://emploi.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/job-offers/lecturer-and-researcher-in-analytic-chemistry-1829925.kjsp?RH=1681202200872": {
      "title": "Lecturer and Researcher in Analytic Chemistry",
      "description": "Lecturer and Researcher in Analytic Chemistry - Emploi - Université Grenoble Alpes Université Grenoble Alpes Practical informations Contacts Campuses map English FR - Français EN - English Job site Welcome Search Open the main menu Open the search engine EN Working at UGA UGA in numbers Recruitment process Careers Senior Lecturers and Professors Fixed-term Contract Faculty Members Temporary Teaching and Research Assistants (ATER) Lecturers and Lecturer-researchers Lecteurs and Maîtres de Langues (Native Speaker Assistants) PhD Students and Researchers Job Offers Competitive Exams Practical informations Contacts Campuses map Université Grenoble Alpes Close the mobile menu FR - Français EN - English Working at UGA Careers Job Offers Competitive Exams LinkedIn Instagram You are here: Home Job Offers Lecturer and Researcher in Analytic Chemistry Response deadline: October 26, 2026 Apply Workload: 100% Employment level: Teacher-researcher Duration of the contract: From December 01, 2026 to August 31, 2027 Location: IUT1 Chimie Gambetta 39 Boulevard Gambetta 38000 Grenoble About the organization The Chemistry Department at IUT1 (UGA) welcomes approximately 100 new students each year. The curricula for BUT1 through BUT3 cover all branches of chemistry (organic, inorganic, materials, analytical, etc). The faculty consists of 25 permanent staff members (faculty researchers and instructors) whose areas of expertise align with the topics taught (in both full-time and work-study programs). Further information on the IUT1 and Chemistry Department websites. LEPMI is a laboratory comprising three teams recognized internationally for their work focused on electrochemistry, materials, and electrochemical engineering. Among these activities, those targeting recycling are among the laboratory's key areas of focus. These activities aim to develop efficient and sustainable recycling methods (particulary for metals and battery materials) within the framework of industrial, academic, and international projects. Further information on LEPMI's website. Your mission Teaching : For teaching assignments focused on analytical chemistry, you will participate in analytical chemistry courses (tutorials and lab sessions) for second and third-year BUT students. Research : You will conduct your research within the LEPMI's EIP team, one of whose flagship projects focuses on the recycling of lithium battery materials (elemental and molecular). Main activities Teaching : You will teach courses focused on analytical chemistry to second-and third-year students in BUT in Chemistry (tutorials and lab sessions), You will have access to a wide range of state-of-the-art analytical instruments (ICP-MS, ICP-AES, SAA, SEA, ion and molecular chomatography, IR and UV spectroscopy, ...). Research : As part of the LEPMI EIP team, you will participate in various funded projects (including industrial partnerships) to assess the effectiveness of recycling. Preferred qualifications You are expected to have the following skills: Pedagogical and scientific expertise in the various branches of chemistry taught. A solid understanding of the phenomena involved in various analytical techniques (both molecular and elemental) in order to critically evaluate measurement sensitivity, accuracy, and interference phenomena. Ability to interact with various people in the department and the laboratory. Diplomas required PhD ou Doctorate Salary Starting at €2194 gross per month, depending on experience. In addition to your salary, you will receive a monthly allowance of €105 gros Apply Published on  October 5, 2026 Updated on  October 5, 2026 For any futher information - About the recruitment process Vaniah RAHARINOSY, recruitment officer lucanne.raharinosy@univ-grenoble-alpes.fr - About the position IUT1 Jean-Claude LEPRETRE, chef du département CHIMIE jean-claude.lepretre@univ-grenoble-alpes.fr +33 (0)6 81 00 46 34 LEPMI Fanny ALLOIN, directrice du laboratoire LEPMI fanny.alloin@grenoble-inp.fr +33 (0)4 76 82 66 98 Why join us Have a meaningfull job Benefit from the attractiveness of the area. Benefit from social adventages. Achieve a good work-life balance. Be accompanied and supported in your career. Work on an inspirative and dynamic. Read more UGA in numbers 57 000 students 10 800 employees 30 academic divisions and units 71 research units, 13 Labex and 7 Equipex www.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr The « HR exellence in research » label The University obtain the HR exellence in research label in April 2021 2021 which was awarded by the European Commission. Read more Print Share Share this on Facebook Share this on LinkedIn Job Offers Université Grenoble Alpes Direction générale déléguée aux Ressources humaines 1180 avenue Centrale 38400 Saint-Martin-d'Hères France +33 (0)4 57 42 21 42 Legal notices Personal data Credits Data protection policy Cookies Accessibility: not compliant Sitemap Follow us LinkedIn Instagram URL of the page https://emploi.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/job-offers/lecturer-and-researcher-in-analytic-chemistry-1829925.kjsp?RH=1681202200872 Page title Share the link Copy Copied Close the modal window Share the URL of this page I recommend: Consultable at this address: La page sera alors accessible depuis votre menu \"Mes favoris\". Stop video Play video Mute Play audio Chat: A question? Chatbot Robo Fabrica Matomo traffic statistics X (formerly Twitter) What are you looking for ? Enter a keyword and press Validate Search on text : More"
